 "drivingQuestion": "Into which domain does the mishna's ledge protrude?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Abaye's reading stands",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "eruvin.98b.7",
   "daf": "98b",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ הַאי זִיז דְּמַפֵּיק לְהֵיכָא? אִילֵּימָא דְּמַפֵּיק לִרְשׁוּת הָרַבִּים — לֵיחוּשׁ דִּילְמָא נָפֵיל, וְאָתֵי לְאֵיתוֹיֵי. אֶלָּא דְּמַפֵּיק לִרְשׁוּת הַיָּחִיד, פְּשִׁיטָא!",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The Gemara clarifies: «This ledge, to where does it protrude? If you say» that the ledge «protrudes into a public domain,» one should be prohibited to place an object on it, as «we should be concerned lest» the object «fall and he» will forget and «come to bring it in» from the public domain to a private domain. «Rather,» it must be «that» the ledge «protrudes into a private domain;» but if so, it is «obvious» that it is permitted to place objects on it and to remove them."
  },
  {
   "id": "eruvin.98b.8",
   "daf": "98b",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "אָמַר אַבָּיֵי: לְעוֹלָם דְּמַפֵּיק לִרְשׁוּת הָרַבִּים, וּמַאי ״נוֹתְנִין עָלָיו״ דְּקָתָנֵי, כֵּלִים הַנִּשְׁבָּרִים.",
   "en": "«Abaye said: Actually,» the mishna is dealing with a case «where it protrudes into a public domain, and what» is the meaning of «that» which «it teaches: One» may «place» objects «upon it?» This refers to «fragile utensils,» which would break instantly if they fell. Consequently, there is no concern that one might then bring them in from the public domain to the private domain."
  }
 ],
